  <ferc:DisclosureOfChangesInOfficersDirectorsMajorSecurityHoldersAndVotingPowersOfTheRespondentTextBlock id="Tag1" contextRef="C1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Joseph Dee was added as a director in July 2025.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfChangesInOfficersDirectorsMajorSecurityHoldersAndVotingPowersOfTheRespondentTextBlock>
  <ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock id="Tag2" contextRef="C1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;!--?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="no"?--&gt;
&lt;div style="widows: 0; orphans: 0;"&gt;
&lt;div class="Section_1"&gt;
&lt;h3 style="margin-top: 8pt; margin-left: 89.95pt; margin-bottom: 4pt; text-indent: -17.95pt; page-break-inside: avoid; page-break-after: avoid; font-size: 14pt; -aw-import: list-item; -aw-list-level-number: 0; -aw-list-number-format: '%0.'; -aw-list-number-styles: 'upperLetter'; -aw-list-number-values: '1'; -aw-list-padding-sml: 7.26pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 11pt; color: #0f4761;"&gt;A.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="width: 7.26pt; font: 7pt 'Times New Roman'; display: inline-block; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: normal; letter-spacing: -0.1pt; color: #0f4761;"&gt;Organization&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin: 0.05pt 18.3pt 0pt 90pt; text-align: justify;"&gt;Mt. Carmel Public Utility Co. (the &amp;#8220;Company&amp;#8221;) was incorporated in the state of Illinois in August 1914. Its principal business is the distribution of natural gas and electricity to the residents and businesses of Wabash County, Illinois.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 style="margin-top: 12.55pt; margin-left: 89.95pt; margin-bottom: 4pt; text-indent: -17.95pt; page-break-inside: avoid; page-break-after: avoid; font-size: 14pt; -aw-import: list-item; -aw-list-level-number: 0; -aw-list-number-format: '%0.'; -aw-list-number-styles: 'upperLetter'; -aw-list-number-values: '2'; -aw-list-padding-sml: 7.86pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 11pt; color: #0f4761;"&gt;B.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="width: 7.86pt; font: 7pt 'Times New Roman'; display: inline-block; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: normal; color: #0f4761;"&gt;System&lt;/font&gt; &lt;font style="font-weight: normal; color: #0f4761;"&gt;of&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: normal; letter-spacing: -0.1pt; color: #0f4761;"&gt; Accounts&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin: 0pt 18.15pt 0pt 90pt; text-align: justify;"&gt;The accounts of the Company are maintained in accordance with the system of accounts prescribed by the Illinois Commerce Commission (the &amp;#8220;ICC&amp;#8221;) and the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission as set forth in its applicable Uniform System of Accounts and published accounting releases, which is a comprehensive basis of accounting other than accounting principles generally accepted in the United States of America.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin: 12.6pt 18.1pt 0pt 90pt; text-align: justify;"&gt;The significant differences between accounting principles generally accepted in the United States of America and those utilized by the Company include: classification of all deferred tax asset and liability accounts on a gross basis as noncurrent; classification of purchased gas and fuel adjustments on a net basis; and classification of certain current liabilities as &lt;font style="letter-spacing: -0.1pt;"&gt;noncurrent.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0.05pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 style="margin-top: 0.05pt; margin-left: 89.95pt; margin-bottom: 4pt; text-indent: -17.95pt; page-break-inside: avoid; page-break-after: avoid; font-size: 14pt; -aw-import: list-item; -aw-list-level-number: 0; -aw-list-number-format: '%0.'; -aw-list-number-styles: 'upperLetter'; -aw-list-number-values: '3'; -aw-list-padding-sml: 7.26pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 11pt; color: #0f4761;"&gt;C.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="width: 7.26pt; font: 7pt 'Times New Roman'; display: inline-block; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: normal; color: #0f4761;"&gt;Use&lt;/font&gt; &lt;font style="font-weight: normal; color: #0f4761;"&gt;of&lt;/font&gt; &lt;font style="font-weight: normal; color: #0f4761;"&gt;Management&lt;/font&gt; &lt;font style="font-weight: normal; letter-spacing: -0.1pt; color: #0f4761;"&gt;Estimates&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin: 0pt 18.1pt 0pt 90pt; text-align: justify;"&gt;The preparation of financial statements in conformity with accounting principles generally accepted in the United States of America requires that management make certain estimates and assumptions that affect the reported amounts of assets and liabilities and disclosure of contingent assets and liabilities at the date of the financial statements. The reported amounts of revenues and expenses during the reporting period may also be affected by the estimates and assumptions management are required to make. Actual results may differ from the estimates.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 style="margin-top: 12.6pt; margin-left: 89.95pt; margin-bottom: 4pt; text-indent: -17.95pt; page-break-inside: avoid; page-break-after: avoid; font-size: 14pt; -aw-import: list-item; -aw-list-level-number: 0; -aw-list-number-format: '%0.'; -aw-list-number-styles: 'upperLetter'; -aw-list-number-values: '4'; -aw-list-padding-sml: 7.26pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 11pt; color: #0f4761;"&gt;D.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="width: 7.26pt; font: 7pt 'Times New Roman'; display: inline-block; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: normal; color: #0f4761;"&gt;Receivables&lt;/font&gt; &lt;font style="font-weight: normal; color: #0f4761;"&gt;and&lt;/font&gt; &lt;font style="font-weight: normal; color: #0f4761;"&gt;Credit&lt;/font&gt; &lt;font style="font-weight: normal; letter-spacing: -0.1pt; color: #0f4761;"&gt;Policies&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0.05pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin: 0pt 18.1pt 0pt 90pt; text-align: justify;"&gt;On January 1, 2023, the Company adopted the new accounting guidance related to the allowance for credit losses on accounts receivable. The impact of adoption of this standard was not material to the financial statements and had no impact on the opening balance of retained earnings. The Company extends credit on a short-term basis to customers in the normal course of business. Accounts receivable are stated at their estimated collectible amounts and comprise amounts billed and currently due from customers. These uncollateralized customer obligations are due under normal trade terms requiring payment within thirty days from the billing date. The carrying amounts of accounts receivable are reduced by an allowance that reflects management&amp;#8217;s best estimate of the amounts that will not be collected. Collections from customers are continuously monitored and an allowance for credit losses is maintained based on historical experience adjusted for current conditions and reasonable forecasts. The Company also considers any specific customer collection issues. Since the Company&amp;#8217;s accounts receivable are largely from utility billings, the Company evaluates its allowance for credit losses as one portfolio segment. At origination, the Company evaluates credit risk based on a variety of credit quality factors including prior payment experience, probabilities of default, and&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin: 0pt 17.8pt 0pt 90pt; text-align: justify;"&gt;other internal metrics. On a continuing basis, data for each major customer is regularly reviewed based on past-due status to evaluate the adequacy of the allowance for credit losses; actual write-offs are charged against the allowance. Write-offs to the allowance for credit losses was $15,406 and $15,406 for the years ended December 31, 2025 and 2024. The balance of accounts receivable as of January 1, 2024 was $871,669.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 style="margin-top: 12.6pt; margin-left: 89.95pt; margin-bottom: 4pt; text-indent: -17.95pt; page-break-inside: avoid; page-break-after: avoid; font-size: 14pt; -aw-import: list-item; -aw-list-level-number: 0; -aw-list-number-format: '%0.'; -aw-list-number-styles: 'upperLetter'; -aw-list-number-values: '5'; -aw-list-padding-sml: 7.86pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 11pt; color: #0f4761;"&gt;E.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="width: 7.86pt; font: 7pt 'Times New Roman'; display: inline-block; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: normal; color: #0f4761;"&gt;Utility&lt;/font&gt; &lt;font style="font-weight: normal; color: #0f4761;"&gt;Plant&lt;/font&gt; &lt;font style="font-weight: normal; color: #0f4761;"&gt;and&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: normal; letter-spacing: -0.1pt; color: #0f4761;"&gt; Depreciation&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin: 0pt 18.2pt 0pt 90pt; text-align: justify;"&gt;Utility plant is stated at original cost. The cost of additions to utility plant includes contracted work, direct labor and materials, and allocable overhead. The cost of units of property retired, replaced, or renewed are removed from utility plant and such costs, plus removal costs, less salvage, are charged to accumulated depreciation. Maintenance and repairs of property and replacement and renewal of items determined to be less than units of property are charged to operating expenses. The Company capitalizes as construction cost an allowance for funds used during construction (&amp;#8220;AFUDC&amp;#8221;), which is defined as the net cost of borrowed funds used for construction purposes and a reasonable return on equity funds when so used. The Company did not capitalize any AFUDC in 2025 or 2024. The equity component of AFUDC is recorded as an item of other income while the interest component is a reduction of interest on long-term debt in the statement of operations and comprehensive income.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin: 12.65pt 18.2pt 0pt 90pt; text-align: justify;"&gt;Depreciation is computed using both the straight-line and the composite methods. The straight-line method is used to determine the depreciation on equipment and buildings. All other depreciation is determined using the composite method at rates approved by the ICC, which are based on the estimated service lives of the various depreciable properties. Such rates were approximately 3% for depreciable electric and gas plants in 2025 and 2024.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0.05pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 style="margin-top: 8pt; margin-left: 89.95pt; margin-bottom: 4pt; text-indent: -17.95pt; page-break-inside: avoid; page-break-after: avoid; font-size: 14pt; -aw-import: list-item; -aw-list-level-number: 0; -aw-list-number-format: '%0.'; -aw-list-number-styles: 'upperLetter'; -aw-list-number-values: '6'; -aw-list-padding-sml: 8.48pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 11pt; color: #0f4761;"&gt;F.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="width: 8.48pt; font: 7pt 'Times New Roman'; display: inline-block; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: normal; color: #0f4761;"&gt;Cash&lt;/font&gt; &lt;font style="font-weight: normal; color: #0f4761;"&gt;and&lt;/font&gt; &lt;font style="font-weight: normal; color: #0f4761;"&gt;Cash&lt;/font&gt; &lt;font style="font-weight: normal; letter-spacing: -0.1pt; color: #0f4761;"&gt;Equivalents&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin: 0pt 18.15pt 0pt 90pt; text-align: justify;"&gt;Cash and cash equivalents include cash on hand and cash in interest-bearing checking accounts, savings accounts, money market accounts, and U.S. treasury notes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 style="margin-top: 8pt; margin-left: 89.95pt; margin-bottom: 4pt; text-indent: -17.95pt; page-break-inside: avoid; page-break-after: avoid; font-size: 14pt; -aw-import: list-item; -aw-list-level-number: 0; -aw-list-number-format: '%0.'; -aw-list-number-styles: 'upperLetter'; -aw-list-number-values: '7'; -aw-list-padding-sml: 6.64pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 11pt; color: #0f4761;"&gt;G.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="width: 6.64pt; font: 7pt 'Times New Roman'; display: inline-block; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: normal; color: #0f4761;"&gt;Gas&lt;/font&gt; &lt;font style="font-weight: normal; color: #0f4761;"&gt;and&lt;/font&gt; &lt;font style="font-weight: normal; color: #0f4761;"&gt;Fuel &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: normal; letter-spacing: -0.2pt; color: #0f4761;"&gt;Costs&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin: 0pt 18.05pt 0pt 90pt; text-align: justify;"&gt;The Company defers over and under recoveries of gas and fuel costs in order to more fully match its revenues and costs. Under the Company&amp;#8217;s Purchased Gas Adjustment (&amp;#8220;PGA&amp;#8221;) clause and electric Fuel Adjustment Clause (&amp;#8220;FAC&amp;#8221;), increases or decreases in gas and fuel costs are passed on to its customers. Accordingly, the difference between the actual costs incurred and the costs recovered through the application of the PGA and FAC are reflected as a deferred charge or credit. Such deferrals are relieved as refunds or additional billings are made.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 style="margin-top: 8pt; margin-left: 89.95pt; margin-bottom: 4pt; text-indent: -17.95pt; page-break-inside: avoid; page-break-after: avoid; font-size: 14pt; -aw-import: list-item; -aw-list-level-number: 0; -aw-list-number-format: '%0.'; -aw-list-number-styles: 'upperLetter'; -aw-list-number-values: '8'; -aw-list-padding-sml: 6.64pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 11pt; color: #0f4761;"&gt;H.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="width: 6.64pt; font: 7pt 'Times New Roman'; display: inline-block; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: normal; color: #0f4761;"&gt;Postretirement&lt;/font&gt; &lt;font style="font-weight: normal; color: #0f4761;"&gt;Benefits&lt;/font&gt; &lt;font style="font-weight: normal; color: #0f4761;"&gt;Other&lt;/font&gt; &lt;font style="font-weight: normal; color: #0f4761;"&gt;Than&lt;/font&gt; &lt;font style="font-weight: normal; letter-spacing: -0.1pt; color: #0f4761;"&gt;Pensions&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin: 0pt 18.25pt 0pt 90pt; text-align: justify;"&gt;The Company accrues the cost for providing postretirement benefits to its employees and their beneficiaries and covered dependents during the years that the employees render the necessary service.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 style="margin-top: 8pt; margin-left: 89.95pt; margin-bottom: 4pt; text-indent: -17.95pt; page-break-inside: avoid; page-break-after: avoid; font-size: 14pt; -aw-import: list-item; -aw-list-level-number: 0; -aw-list-number-format: '%0.'; -aw-list-number-styles: 'upperLetter'; -aw-list-number-values: '9'; -aw-list-padding-sml: 10.92pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 11pt; color: #0f4761;"&gt;I.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="width: 10.92pt; font: 7pt 'Times New Roman'; display: inline-block; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: normal; color: #0f4761;"&gt;Income&lt;/font&gt; &lt;font style="font-weight: normal; letter-spacing: -0.1pt; color: #0f4761;"&gt;Taxes&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin: 0.05pt 18.2pt 0pt 90pt; text-align: justify;"&gt;The Company uses an asset-liability approach to measuring the impact of income taxes and recognizes deferred tax assets or liabilities based upon temporary differences in the tax basis of an asset or liability and its related financial statement balance. The deferred tax asset or liability is calculated using the enacted tax rates expected to apply in the period in which the deferred asset or liability is expected to be settled or realized.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 style="margin-top: 12.55pt; margin-left: 89.95pt; margin-bottom: 4pt; text-indent: -17.95pt; page-break-inside: avoid; page-break-after: avoid; font-size: 14pt; -aw-import: list-item; -aw-list-level-number: 0; -aw-list-number-format: '%0.'; -aw-list-number-styles: 'upperLetter'; -aw-list-number-values: '10'; -aw-list-padding-sml: 9.7pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 11pt; color: #0f4761;"&gt;J.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="width: 9.7pt; font: 7pt 'Times New Roman'; display: inline-block; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: normal; letter-spacing: -0.1pt; color: #0f4761;"&gt;Revenues&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0.05pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin: 0pt 18.1pt 0pt 90pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;The Company &lt;font style="font-size: 11pt;"&gt;records revenues from contracts with customers for various electric and natural gas services, which primarily consist of retail distribution, electric transmission, and off-system arrangements. When more than one performance obligation exists in a contract, the consideration under the contract is allocated to the performance obligations based on the relative standalone selling price.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin: 0pt 18.1pt 0pt 90pt; text-align: justify;"&gt;Electric and natural gas retail distribution revenues are earned when the commodity is delivered to our customers. Electric transmission revenues are earned as electric transmission services are provided. Off-system revenues are primarily comprised of MISO revenues. MISO revenues include the sale of electricity, capacity, and ancillary services. MISO-related electricity revenues are earned as electricity is delivered. Capacity and ancillary service revenues are earned as services are provided.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin: 0pt 18.15pt 0pt 90pt; text-align: justify;"&gt;Retail distribution, electric transmission, and off-system revenues, including the underlying components described above, represent a series of goods or services that are substantially the same and have the same pattern of transfer over time to our customers. Revenues from contracts with customers are equal to the amounts billed. Customers are billed at least monthly, and payments are due less than one month after goods and/or services are provided.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin: 0pt 18.15pt 0pt 90pt; text-align: justify;"&gt;As of December 31, 2025 and 2024, our remaining performance obligations were immaterial. The Company elected not to disclose the aggregate amount of the transaction price allocated to the performance obligations that are unsatisfied as of the end of the reporting period for contracts with an initial expected term of one year or less.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 style="margin-top: 8pt; margin-left: 89.95pt; margin-bottom: 4pt; text-indent: -17.95pt; page-break-inside: avoid; page-break-after: avoid; font-size: 14pt; -aw-import: list-item; -aw-list-level-number: 0; -aw-list-number-format: '%0.'; -aw-list-number-styles: 'upperLetter'; -aw-list-number-values: '11'; -aw-list-padding-sml: 6.64pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 11pt; color: #0f4761;"&gt;K.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="width: 6.64pt; font: 7pt 'Times New Roman'; display: inline-block; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: normal; color: #0f4761;"&gt;Earnings&lt;/font&gt; &lt;font style="font-weight: normal; color: #0f4761;"&gt;per&lt;/font&gt; &lt;font style="font-weight: normal; color: #0f4761;"&gt;Share&lt;/font&gt; &lt;font style="font-weight: normal; color: #0f4761;"&gt;of&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: normal; letter-spacing: -0.1pt; color: #0f4761;"&gt; Stock&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p style="margin: 12.55pt 18.4pt 0pt 90pt; text-align: justify;"&gt;Earnings per share of stock are computed using the weighted-average number of common shares outstanding during the applicable period.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&amp;#160;&amp;#160;
&lt;div class="Section_2"&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 style="margin-top: 8pt; margin-left: 89.95pt; margin-bottom: 4pt; text-indent: -17.95pt; page-break-inside: avoid; page-break-after: avoid; font-size: 14pt; -aw-import: list-item; -aw-list-level-number: 0; -aw-list-number-format: '%0.'; -aw-list-number-styles: 'upperLetter'; -aw-list-number-values: '12'; -aw-list-padding-sml: 7.86pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 11pt; color: #0f4761;"&gt;L.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="width: 7.86pt; font: 7pt 'Times New Roman'; display: inline-block; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: normal; color: #0f4761;"&gt;Asset&lt;/font&gt; &lt;font style="font-weight: normal; letter-spacing: -0.1pt; color: #0f4761;"&gt;Retirements&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin: 0.05pt 17.8pt 0pt 90pt; text-align: justify;"&gt;The Financial Accounting Standards Board (&amp;#8220;FASB&amp;#8221;) ASC 410-20, &lt;font style="font-style: italic;"&gt;Accounting for Asset Retirement Obligations, &lt;/font&gt;addresses financial accounting and reporting for obligations associated with the retirement of tangible long-lived assets and associated asset retirement costs. It applies to legal obligations associated with the retirement of long-lived assets that result from acquisition, construction, development, and/or the normal operation of a long-lived asset, except for certain obligations of lessees. The provisions of the statement provide for rate-regulated entities that meet the criteria for application of FASB ASC 980-10, &lt;font style="font-style: italic;"&gt;Accounting for the Effects of Certain Types of Regulation&lt;/font&gt;, such as the Company, to recognize regulatory assets or liabilities for differences in the timing of recognition of the period costs associated with asset retirement obligations for financial reporting pursuant to this statement and rate-making purposes. Accordingly, the Company has recorded asset retirement obligations related to legal obligations to dispose of certain assets included in the Company&amp;#8217;s distribution and transmission systems upon final abandonment of the systems. This liability was $352,788 and $340,864 as of 12/31/2025 and 2024, &lt;font style="letter-spacing: -0.1pt;"&gt;respectively.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 style="margin-top: 12.55pt; margin-left: 89.95pt; margin-bottom: 4pt; text-indent: -17.95pt; page-break-inside: avoid; page-break-after: avoid; font-size: 14pt; -aw-import: list-item; -aw-list-level-number: 0; -aw-list-number-format: '%0.'; -aw-list-number-styles: 'upperLetter'; -aw-list-number-values: '13'; -aw-list-padding-sml: 4.82pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 11pt; color: #0f4761;"&gt;M.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="width: 4.82pt; font: 7pt 'Times New Roman'; display: inline-block; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: normal; color: #0f4761;"&gt;Comprehensive&lt;/font&gt; &lt;font style="font-weight: normal; color: #0f4761;"&gt;Income&lt;/font&gt; &lt;font style="font-weight: normal; letter-spacing: -0.1pt; color: #0f4761;"&gt;(Loss)&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin: 0.05pt 18.05pt 0pt 90pt; text-align: justify;"&gt;The Company follows the provisions of FASB ASC 220-10, &lt;font style="font-style: italic;"&gt;Reporting Comprehensive Income&lt;/font&gt;, which governs the financial statement presentation of changes in shareholder&amp;#8217;s equity resulting from non-owner sources. Accumulated other comprehensive income (loss) as reported in the accompanying statements of changes in stockholders&amp;#8217; equity represents unrealized gains and losses on deferred pension and other postretirement costs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 style="margin-top: 12.6pt; margin-left: 89.95pt; margin-bottom: 4pt; text-indent: -17.95pt; page-break-inside: avoid; page-break-after: avoid; font-size: 14pt; -aw-import: list-item; -aw-list-level-number: 0; -aw-list-number-format: '%0.'; -aw-list-number-styles: 'upperLetter'; -aw-list-number-values: '14'; -aw-list-padding-sml: 7.26pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 11pt; color: #0f4761;"&gt;N.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="width: 7.26pt; font: 7pt 'Times New Roman'; display: inline-block; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: normal; letter-spacing: -0.1pt; color: #0f4761;"&gt;Concentrations&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin: 0pt 18.3pt 0pt 90pt; text-align: justify;"&gt;The Company maintains cash balances in various financial institutions. These balances are insured by the Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation (FDIC) up to $250,000. At December 31, 2025 and 2024, the uninsured portion of these balances was $84,111 &lt;font style="letter-spacing: -0.25pt;"&gt;and&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 90pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 12.6pt;"&gt;$530,263, &lt;font style="letter-spacing: -0.1pt;"&gt;respectively.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin: 0pt 18.2pt 0pt 90pt; text-align: justify;"&gt;The Company acquires the majority of natural gas and electricity from a single natural gas supplier and a single electricity supplier. An interruption of service from either or both of these suppliers could affect operating results.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0.05pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin: 0pt 18.2pt 0pt 90pt; text-align: justify;"&gt;The Company&amp;#8217;s gas and electrical workforce is covered under a collective bargaining agreement that expires on October 20, 2027. The Company&amp;#8217;s other employees are not represented by a union.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 12.6pt; margin-left: 90pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify;"&gt;Customers of the Company are primarily located in Wabash County, &lt;font style="letter-spacing: -0.1pt;"&gt;Illinois.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 style="margin-top: 8pt; margin-left: 89.95pt; margin-bottom: 4pt; text-indent: -17.95pt; page-break-inside: avoid; page-break-after: avoid; font-size: 14pt; -aw-import: list-item; -aw-list-level-number: 0; -aw-list-number-format: '%0.'; -aw-list-number-styles: 'upperLetter'; -aw-list-number-values: '15'; -aw-list-padding-sml: 6.64pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 11pt; color: #0f4761;"&gt;O.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="width: 6.64pt; font: 7pt 'Times New Roman'; display: inline-block; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: normal; color: #0f4761;"&gt;Utility&lt;/font&gt; &lt;font style="font-weight: normal; letter-spacing: -0.1pt; color: #0f4761;"&gt;Taxes&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0.05pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin: 0pt 18.15pt 0pt 90pt; text-align: justify;"&gt;Taxes collected on behalf of state and local governments are presented under the gross method in the statement of operations and comprehensive income.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 style="margin-top: 8pt; margin-left: 89.95pt; margin-bottom: 4pt; text-indent: -17.95pt; page-break-inside: avoid; page-break-after: avoid; font-size: 14pt; -aw-import: list-item; -aw-list-level-number: 0; -aw-list-number-format: '%0.'; -aw-list-number-styles: 'upperLetter'; -aw-list-number-values: '16'; -aw-list-padding-sml: 8.48pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 11pt; color: #0f4761;"&gt;P.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="width: 8.48pt; font: 7pt 'Times New Roman'; display: inline-block; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: normal; letter-spacing: -0.1pt; color: #0f4761;"&gt;Inventory&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin: 0.05pt 18.1pt 0pt 90pt; text-align: justify;"&gt;Inventory consists of replacement materials for use in gas and electric distribution. Inventory is stated at the lower of cost or net realizable value on the first in, first out method. Items placed in service are capitalized when installed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 style="margin-top: 12.55pt; margin-left: 89.95pt; margin-bottom: 4pt; text-indent: -17.95pt; page-break-inside: avoid; page-break-after: avoid; font-size: 14pt; -aw-import: list-item; -aw-list-level-number: 0; -aw-list-number-format: '%0.'; -aw-list-number-styles: 'upperLetter'; -aw-list-number-values: '17'; -aw-list-padding-sml: 6.64pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 11pt; color: #0f4761;"&gt;Q.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="width: 6.64pt; font: 7pt 'Times New Roman'; display: inline-block; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: normal; color: #0f4761;"&gt;Date&lt;/font&gt; &lt;font style="font-weight: normal; color: #0f4761;"&gt;of&lt;/font&gt; &lt;font style="font-weight: normal; color: #0f4761;"&gt;Management&amp;#8217;s&lt;/font&gt; &lt;font style="font-weight: normal; letter-spacing: -0.1pt; color: #0f4761;"&gt;Review&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin: 0pt 18.25pt 0pt 90pt; text-align: justify;"&gt;Management has evaluated subsequent events through March 12, 2026, the date which the financial statements were available to be issued.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock>
